abstract: >-
  World 7 is a ratification-candidate genomic runtime architecture for persistent
  digital organisms. It separates identity, canonical state, memory, authority,
  lineage, development, genesis, repair, reconstruction and evolution from
  replaceable AI models and providers. The v0.2 candidate defines a 19-domain
  Universal Genome, governed inheritance and birth gates, RoleBinding-based
  authority, a deterministic proposal-to-commit Spine with CAS, idempotency and
  hash chaining, Pulse/Tempo/Resolution controls, and an evidence-driven G0 to
  G10 growth path beginning with secretary-001. The evidence boundary is explicit:
  2048 proof obligations are registered, 4096/4096 bounded local assertions and
  18/18 seed reference tests pass, while live shared ChatGPT/Grok canonical state,
  clean-host restore, PostgreSQL atomicity, security/load/chaos and production
  readiness remain open.
